# Flipkart E-Commerce Product Analysis Using Python
1. Project Overview

This project analyzes a Flipkart e-commerce product dataset using Python to understand product performance, pricing, discounts, sales volume, customer ratings, seller performance, and other operational attributes.

The analysis was performed on 80,000 product records containing 25 original variables. Python libraries including Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, and Seaborn were used for data inspection, preprocessing, feature engineering, statistical analysis, and exploratory data analysis.

2. Objectives

The main objectives of this analysis were to:

Understand the structure and quality of the Flipkart product dataset.
Identify missing values and duplicate records.
Prepare the data for analysis.
Create additional analytical variables.
Analyze product pricing and discount patterns.
Identify top-selling products.
Compare categories based on estimated revenue.
Analyze discount levels against units sold.
Evaluate seller performance using product scores.
Examine relationships between ratings and sales.
Investigate whether delivery time, return policy, and product weight are associated with sales.
Identify products with high ratings but low sales.
